{
  "description": "Round 269 on arena/01a10bfd-git-pull-arena: finish the last-page swap and prove it. image-1.jpeg is a photograph of page 6 of this document, signed and stamped; page 6 of the docx is that same form left blank, so 'replace the last page' means make the scan BE page 6 with the document still 6 pages and pages 1-5 untouched. Round 268 already did the edit correctly (6 -> 6 pages, image fitted to 453x651.6pt) but its receipt was destroyed by a PowerShell trap: variable names are case-insensitive, so 'foreach ($l in $lines)' overwrote the $L report buffer, and the prefix hash counted the inserted page-break character as a content change. Both are fixed - the buffer is renamed, pages 1-5 are now compared on visible text only, and code/scan_ps_case_shadow.py is wired into code/check_all.sh so a loop variable can never again clobber another variable by case alone. 'Local' means that machine's scheduled watcher - never a sandbox folder. The v2.8.1 skill, the alias-shadow gate, code/local_check.ps1 and every deliverable inherited from earlier rounds stay in force.",
